Maintainer: Giorgio Alfredo Spedicato <spedicato_giorgio@yahoo.it>
Description: Description: Functions and S4 classes to create, manage and analyse discrete
    time Markov chains. Includes probabilistic analysis of chain structure
    (state classification, hitting times, stationary distributions, spectral
    and mixing diagnostics), statistical inference (maximum likelihood and
    Bayesian estimation, tests of the Markov property, homogeneity, stationarity
    and order, simulation), higher-order and multivariate chains, state
    aggregation, and import/export to JSON, YAML and CSV. Basic support for
    continuous time Markov chains is also provided; some of these functions
    depend on the suggested 'ctmcd' package.
    See Spedicato (2017) <doi:10.32614/RJ-2017-036>.
